        <updated>2026-03-31T00:00:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69cb9dc54281a15b20edbfff_Axios%20%20-%20social-1.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69cb9dc54281a15b20edbfff_Axios%20%20-%20social-1-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69cb9dc54281a15b20edbfff_Axios%20%20-%20social-1-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69cb9dc54281a15b20edbfff_Axios%20%20-%20social-1-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/69cb9dc54281a15b20edbfff_Axios%20%20-%20social-1.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">Cloud Security</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AI SOC</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-0" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%2269cb9de426d52826832cc184%22%7D%5D" href="/post/axios-compromised-the-2-hour-window-between-detection-and-damage" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">Axios Compromised: The 2-Hour Window Between Detection and Damage</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">Hours ago, axios - one of the most popular npm packages with 60M+ weekly downloads - was compromised. Malicious versions dropped a multi-platform RAT with anti-forensic cleanup. This is the second major supply chain attack in a week, days after TeamPCP's Trivy/LiteLLM campaign. The CI/CD scanner side of this story is well-documented. This post is about what happens after the malware runs - because that's where most organizations actually fail.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Petr Zuzanov" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png" sizes="70px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png 1400w" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Petr Zuzanov</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs w-condition-invisible"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">Mar 31, 2026</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
