        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6984fc4cf5515de9ef76982c_openclaw-%20cover.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6984fc4cf5515de9ef76982c_openclaw-%20cover-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6984fc4cf5515de9ef76982c_openclaw-%20cover-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6984fc4cf5515de9ef76982c_openclaw-%20cover-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6984fc4cf5515de9ef76982c_openclaw-%20cover.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">AI</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AI SOC</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CloudTwin</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CDR</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-3" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%226984fc208c0c97b6b0e70ae1%22%7D%5D" href="/post/the-hidden-fragility-of-autonomous-ai-systems" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">The Hidden Fragility of Autonomous AI Systems</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">AI oversight collapsed in steps as systems became "good enough." We got speed but lost resilience. Errors now accumulate silently and surface after dependencies compound. Adding more AI to the SOC accelerates this problem. The fix is architectural: a continuously updated model of your environment that knows what's true now.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Or Shoshani" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68766b2e27adca47f2d2e213_OR.webp" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Or Shoshani</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">Feb 6, 2026</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
<g clip-path="url(#clip0_2629_8)">
