        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/694a77a2af5a4fdfa56fcab4_blog%20cover.png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/694a77a2af5a4fdfa56fcab4_blog%20cover-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/694a77a2af5a4fdfa56fcab4_blog%20cover-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/694a77a2af5a4fdfa56fcab4_blog%20cover-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/694a77a2af5a4fdfa56fcab4_blog%20cover.png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">Cloud Security</div><div class="highlight-tag pop w-condition-invisible">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AI SOC</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">AWS</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CDR</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CloudTwin</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">Disaster Recovery</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-7" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%2268d63c2d750034897491583b%22%7D%5D" href="/post/is-your-soc-team-ready-to-pass-cloud-kyc" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">Is Your SOC Team Ready to Pass Cloud KYC?</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">If you don’t know your cloud, you can’t secure it. Alerts and AI don’t help much without real context. “Know Your Cloud” (KYC) is about understanding what you actually have, who and what can access it, and what could go wrong. Get that right, and detection makes sense, AI gets smarter, and response gets better.</div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Stream Team" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/67cf5e9a8c818ec67007d051_Large%20favicon3.webp" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Stream Team</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">Dec 29, 2025</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
